# Environment variables for the FounderLab website. Copy to .env.local for local work.
# Placeholders only: never commit real values. On Vercel, set these in Project Settings ->
# Environment Variables (Production and Preview as needed).

# --- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Renor Guide: AI answers (optional) ------------------------------------------------------
# Without these the Guide runs in offline mode: instant answers from its curated knowledge
# base, plus the report form. Set RECEPTIONIST_MODEL and either a provider preset or a base URL
# to switch on AI answers. Any OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint works.
#
# Free tiers:
#   Gemini: RECEPTIONIST_PROVIDER=gemini, key from aistudio.google.com, e.g. a Flash model id
#   Groq:   RECEPTIONIST_PROVIDER=groq,   key from console.groq.com
# The founder's own local model through a tunnel or the company gateway:
#   RECEPTIONIST_BASE_URL=https://<your-tunnel-host>/v1   (https required outside localhost)
RECEPTIONIST_PROVIDER=
RECEPTIONIST_BASE_URL=
RECEPTIONIST_API_KEY=
RECEPTIONIST_MODEL=
# Optional per-call ceiling in milliseconds (2000-60000, default 15000).
RECEPTIONIST_TIMEOUT_MS=

# --- Renor Guide: private report store (optional) --------------------------------------------
# Reports are stored privately server-side, never posted to GitHub or any public tracker.
# Without a store, each report is handed back to the visitor as a filled-in email (mailto).
# Store: an Upstash Redis database (free tier; also available via the Vercel Marketplace).
# Use its REST URL and a read-write REST token. Used for reports only.
REPORTS_KV_REST_URL=
REPORTS_KV_REST_TOKEN=
# Days before a report is deleted automatically (1-365, default 90). The privacy page says 90:
# update it if you change this.
REPORTS_RETENTION_DAYS=
# Local development only: keep reports in server memory (lost on restart; ignored in production).
# REPORTS_STORE=memory

# --- Renor Guide: team triage page (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# /admin/reports lists stored reports, grouped by problem, with severity, area and steps.
# It is off (404) until this is set. Use a long random value (at least 24 characters), e.g.
# `openssl rand -base64 32`, and share it only with the team.
REPORTS_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# --- Renor Guide: engineering hand-off (optional, OFF by default) --------------------------------
# When both are set, each stored report also POSTs a PII-free summary (type, severity, area, page,
# group size; the visitor's redacted words only if they agreed) to a private endpoint you control,
# signed with HMAC-SHA256 in the `x-renor-signature: sha256=<hex>` header. https only.
REPORTS_HANDOFF_URL=
REPORTS_HANDOFF_SECRET=
